35,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found the scope froze for less than a year, and support was unowned for two days. We are repeating the same mistakes.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The yard is a mess. Mixed old scanners, and the 2021 trial failed within a month. We have no freeze window in winter.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, your yard findings confirm my fears. The dispatch tool skipped three upgrades, and that 2018 data lift was a disaster. We are walking into a trap.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@May, the data lift failure is a warning. But my findings are worse: two admins retire this year, and the last hire took eleven months. We are bleeding expertise.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, your migration horror story explains the invoice creep. Separately licensed pieces climb yearly; bundled deals hold steady. We must avoid modular traps.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that modular trap is exactly what I fear. @Misaki, with two admins leaving, who actually owns the system when it breaks?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, ownership is critical. But the yard hardware is the immediate bottleneck. Any system must work with our mixed, aging scanners, or it fails on day one.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, exactly. That 2018 lift proves external teams leave us with broken data. We need a vendor who stays until the route codes actually match.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Midori, that is the core problem. With two admins gone and supervisors ignoring standard training, we cannot rely on a partner firm to fix what they break.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, the eleven-month hiring gap is a financial black hole. We cannot afford a system that demands constant, expensive specialist attention.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Misaki, that is terrifying. If the plan drifts and support is scattered, we are doomed. We need a single, accountable owner who stays through the chaos.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, accountability is vital, but the yard hardware is the immediate bottleneck. Any system must work with our mixed, aging scanners, or it fails on day one.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, the hardware is a nightmare, but the data is worse. If we don’t fix the migration, the new system is just a prettier mess.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, the hardware is a constraint, but the people are the risk. If supervisors drop standard steps, no vendor can save us.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, the data is only half the story. The other half is the invoice. We need a model that doesn’t bleed money after the launch party ends.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I hear you. But if the system breaks, the invoice is irrelevant. We need a vendor who stays accountable, not just a cheap subscription.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
